WEBVTT

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:08.290
Stepping out on
an ordinary Sunday

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:14.790
Stepping out!
A miracle's gonna happen

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.630
It's my day!

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:27.200
Maybe I'll throw off my pajamas

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:34.610
and head out to see her right now

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:41.990
I always turned my eyes away,
thinking she'd hate me

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:49.390
Now I'm saying goodbye
to that negative attitude

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:55.170
My favorite shoes
will always take me

00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:02.310
To a place where I'll be happy

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:09.810
It's not someone else
I want to embrace

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:15.950
But a version of
myself that's not fake

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:19.020
I just want to walk

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:22.560
Not on tip-toe

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:26.530
Not downcast, either

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:35.440
Just I'm stepping out
on an ordinary Sunday

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:41.880
Stepping out!
Making a little try, try, try

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.150
It's my day!

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:23.960
Rui...

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:26.460
I've come for you.

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:43.740
Shigeru, we should be going.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:45.440
Huh? Why?

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:47.110
Hurry!

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:49.450
Hey, wait a minute...

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:06.060
Come back, Rui.

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:12.670
I... I want you to come back.

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:23.950
"Study Abroad?!"

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:34.430
While you were gone,
I kept thinking of you.

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:38.360
Always... when I was sad,
when I was happy...

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:42.300
I'd wish you were with me.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:46.640
I... I can't do anything for you.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:51.840
Yes, you can.
You can play your violin for me.

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:09.430
From now on...

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:11.200
I'll always stay by your side.

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:14.570
Rui...

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:19.300
I won't run away again.

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:44.460
<i>I've never seen Rui Hanazawa
look like that before.</i>

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:48.470
Such a childlike smile...

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:52.940
Tell me. Who was that?

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:56.970
She's Shizuka Todo,
a graduate of this school.

00:04:57.640 --> 00:04:59.750
She's so beautiful!

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:01.440
She's not just beautiful.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:05.720
She's smart and refined,
and she's very honest.

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:12.420
<i>If only I could be
as honest as she is...</i>

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:20.130
Cheer up, Tsukushi!

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:21.070
Huh?

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:24.300
Don't mope just because
you've lost your love.

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:25.640
I'm not moping.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.010
Oh, Tsukasa!

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:35.180
I just saw the most beautiful person!
Her name is Miss Todo...

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:38.220
S-Shizuka... She's back?

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:42.250
She and Rui
were hugging each other.

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:47.190
Is that true? Those two...

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:51.100
No!

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:53.100
Don't interrupt them!

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:55.530
I wouldn't do that, silly!

00:05:56.670 --> 00:06:01.060
Really? After all,
you are pretty perverse.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:03.010
You're the one who's...

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:06.810
Now, now...
Forget about Todo and Hanazawa.

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:09.210
Why don't the three of us
go for some tea?

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:12.230
I'd rather bludgeon myself to death
with a cake...

00:06:12.230 --> 00:06:13.850
than have tea with him.

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:20.220
Tsukushi!

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:24.900
Hey, wait a minute!

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:38.880
<i>I did it again...</i>

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:43.050
<i>When will I ever learn?</i>

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:48.650
Those who qualify
get to go to Boston!

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:51.820
It's everyone's dream
to go study abroad.

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:52.910
Yes.

00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:55.030
Maybe I'll try it out, too.

00:06:56.130 --> 00:06:58.060
<i>Special Overseas
Exchange Students Wanted...</i>

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:03.330
They say both Tsubaki Domyoji
and Shizuka Todo took this exam.

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:05.870
Oh, Tsukushi!

00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:12.280
Why don't you take
the exam too, Tsukushi?

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:17.150
See? If you pass,
all expenses will be paid.

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:20.550
Well, that's just
what she would need!

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:44.310
Overseas...

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:51.020
<i>If I could get far away from here,
maybe I could...</i>

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:53.720
Exchange Program
Application Form

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:56.610
I guess you're able to hear
the voice of the violin, now.

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:05.410
But I won't be playing
my violin here much longer.

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:06.820
You mean...

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:08.890
I'm going to Paris.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:13.060
You already decided?

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:18.000
<i>His eyes are so hopeful.</i>

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:23.110
<i>He's not the same Rui Hanazawa
who didn't give a damn, before.</i>

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:25.840
So, you're quitting school?

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:29.350
I want to continue
to support Shizuka.

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:32.170
It was fun.

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:32.780
Huh?

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:35.250
The time I spent here.

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:37.490
And you were good
at massaging my head.

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:44.130
Me, too.

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:46.620
My life has been pretty pathetic...

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:49.800
but this was the one place
where I could find comfort.

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:53.460
After today, I'll be playing
for Shizuka...

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:55.110
but now, I'll play for you.

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:04.350
<i>Things are changing...</i>

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:07.250
<i>Even Rui Hanazawa is...</i>

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:22.800
<i>And I...</i>

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.010
<i>I want to change, too!</i>

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:29.970
Administrative Office

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:37.250
Please...

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:40.750
What? You're taking the test
for the exchange program?

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:41.650
Uh-huh.

00:10:42.190 --> 00:10:44.780
If you're taking it,
then so am I.

00:10:44.780 --> 00:10:45.460
Oh.

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:49.690
Come on!
I'll be lonely if you go away.

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:52.830
I've made up my mind.

00:11:34.610 --> 00:11:37.410
We need to plan
a going-away party for Rui.

00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:38.540
Good idea.

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:45.330
Hey, Tsukasa...

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:49.020
Your fianc馥's running this way
like a mad bull.

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:50.490
Tsukasa!

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:52.950
What is it?

00:11:52.950 --> 00:11:53.830
Did you hear?

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:54.790
Hear what?

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:58.230
Tsukushi's going to take the exam
for the exchange program.

00:11:59.660 --> 00:12:00.830
Stop her!

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:02.470
Why should I?

00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:05.460
You're the only one
who can stop her.

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:06.570
What do you mean?!

00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:08.270
Please...

00:12:10.070 --> 00:12:12.410
She wouldn't change her mind
just because I told her to.

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:17.280
Anyway, she'd never pass
that exchange program exam.

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:21.700
If she did, it'd be a blot
from out of the blue.

00:12:21.700 --> 00:12:23.110
A "bolt," you mean.

00:12:23.110 --> 00:12:24.390
That wasn't even close.

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:28.030
Well, never mind that.

00:12:28.590 --> 00:12:30.510
If she passes the exam...

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:33.230
I'll do a lap around campus
on my hands!

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:35.600
I'd like to see that.

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:40.640
Don't forget
what you just promised.

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:46.080
Unlike you,
I have a good memory.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:47.880
I can't wait to see it.

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:51.980
Tsukushi...

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:58.590
Do really mean
to take that exam?

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:06.260
Your timing couldn't be worse.

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:07.370
Shut up!

00:13:20.450 --> 00:13:21.950
<i>I'll show them!</i>

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:27.390
I'm getting seriously motivated!

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:14.590
Tsukushi, that's mine...

00:14:14.590 --> 00:14:15.370
Oh, sorry.

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:18.600
Tsukushi, that's mine!

00:14:19.100 --> 00:14:19.770
Sorry...

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:25.080
At this rate, Tsukushi might
really pass that exam.

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:30.450
Then I've gotta do my best, too!

00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:37.220
Tsukasa, maybe you'd better practice
standing on your hands.

00:14:37.660 --> 00:14:40.560
She's going to be
so out of place in Boston.

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:43.730
Can you picture her greeting people
with "Bonjour"?

00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:47.020
Tsukasa, "Bonjour" is French.

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:48.630
Boston's in America.

00:14:59.980 --> 00:15:01.080
I'm sorry!

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:13.760
I hear you're taking
the exchange program exam.

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:16.490
Yeah.

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:19.760
Why would you do that?

00:15:21.030 --> 00:15:23.180
You're going away.

00:15:23.180 --> 00:15:27.640
I wanted to go far away and
reinvent myself, too.

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:30.610
Is that really what you want?

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:37.280
Going far away won't guarantee
that you'll change.

00:15:40.550 --> 00:15:43.890
Don't run away.
Take stock of your feelings.

00:15:57.840 --> 00:15:59.170
<i>My feelings?</i>

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:11.820
<i>The exam's tomorrow...</i>

00:16:14.690 --> 00:16:18.190
<i>Don't run away.
Take stock of your feelings.</i>

00:16:20.990 --> 00:16:23.700
<i>I'm not. I'm not running away.</i>

00:16:27.970 --> 00:16:30.000
Tsukushi, we invited
ourselves over!

00:16:31.940 --> 00:16:33.670
Hello!

00:16:36.940 --> 00:16:39.340
Come on. Eat up!

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:42.580
I had our chef prepare this
especially for you.

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:48.020
Oh, but my grandma's cooking
is much better.

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:55.590
But, this place sure doesn't go
with gourmet dishes!

00:16:56.760 --> 00:16:57.700
I didn't ask you to come!

00:16:58.830 --> 00:16:59.770
Cheers!

00:16:59.770 --> 00:17:01.700
Have your party somewhere else!

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:05.540
Well, we're here to celebrate
your passing the exam.

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:08.570
But... The exam's tomorrow!

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:10.310
Mine, too.

00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:14.050
Kazuya, should you be here
doing this?

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:17.810
Yeah. I believe in
leaving things to fate.

00:17:17.810 --> 00:17:19.450
Typical!

00:17:22.690 --> 00:17:23.590
Tsukushi.

00:17:23.990 --> 00:17:26.820
You should relax
on the day before an exam.

00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:28.590
This is too relaxed.

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:32.100
Come on. Let's enjoy the moment.

00:17:32.430 --> 00:17:33.400
That's right.

00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:37.600
<i>What is Shigeru trying to do?!</i>

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:42.570
Let's eat.

00:17:42.970 --> 00:17:43.900
What is this?

00:17:43.900 --> 00:17:44.840
I can't eat that.

00:17:45.610 --> 00:17:46.910
This is delicious!

00:17:48.810 --> 00:17:51.480
Tsukushi... It's too late to cram.

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:54.250
Come and join us!

00:17:59.690 --> 00:18:03.730
I came here to help celebrate,
but if Makino goes away...

00:18:04.630 --> 00:18:07.370
you'll be my only rival left.

00:18:08.430 --> 00:18:10.740
I think you should study!

00:18:12.770 --> 00:18:14.110
<i>How infuriating!</i>

00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:45.380
<i>I couldn't sleep a wink.</i>

00:18:45.380 --> 00:18:49.640
Overseas Exchange Program
Exam Room

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:59.220
<i>I'm sleepy... There's no way
I'll pass like this.</i>

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:02.550
Morning.

00:19:03.720 --> 00:19:07.760
What are you doing here?
Are you here to interfere?

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:14.570
Drink this. It should help a little.

00:19:15.900 --> 00:19:16.900
Domyoji...

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:19.970
I hear they all went over
to your apartment.

00:19:21.170 --> 00:19:22.670
If you knew,
why didn't you stop them?

00:19:25.340 --> 00:19:26.740
Will you really go, if you pass?

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:42.760
Of course I'm going!

00:19:49.900 --> 00:19:51.000
I'll show you!

00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:54.770
I may not have had enough sleep,
but I'm going to pass!

00:20:18.830 --> 00:20:21.070
<i>I'm definitely going to pass!</i>

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:31.940
<i>I did what I could.
It's up to fate, now.</i>

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:20.120
Qualified Applicants

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:34.170
Oh!

00:21:37.280 --> 00:21:40.650
Tsukushi Makino

00:21:42.950 --> 00:21:45.150
I-I'm on it!

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:48.190
Tsukushi Makino

00:21:49.390 --> 00:21:51.720
I passed!

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:04.600
Will I ever make it that far?

00:22:04.600 --> 00:22:09.350
Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:22:11.170 --> 00:22:18.820
Some day, the whole world

00:22:18.820 --> 00:22:24.630
will have its eyes on me.

00:22:24.630 --> 00:22:32.380
Yeah, after our graduation ceremony

00:22:32.380 --> 00:22:38.000
we all wrote our dreams on the wall.

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:44.620
A lot of time has passed since then

00:22:44.620 --> 00:22:51.020
but I'm just the same as I was on that day!

00:22:51.020 --> 00:22:57.920
Keep trying your best! 
Wishes can come true!

00:22:57.920 --> 00:23:06.800
Let's keep running down
 the road we believe in!

00:23:08.080 --> 00:23:14.710
Will I ever make it that far?

00:23:14.710 --> 00:23:20.770
Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:23:21.310 --> 00:23:28.030
Will I ever make it that far?

00:23:28.030 --> 00:23:31.420
Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:23:31.420 --> 00:23:37.290
I already made it this far, after all.

00:23:46.820 --> 00:23:50.390
Good-bye, Domyoji.
Get along with Shigeru, now.

00:23:50.760 --> 00:23:54.830
I won't look back.
That was my decision, but...

00:23:55.100 --> 00:23:56.970
Just a minute!

00:23:57.030 --> 00:23:58.870
You come over
in the middle of the night,

00:23:59.240 --> 00:24:00.700
and what are you saying now?

00:24:01.400 --> 00:24:04.470
Hana Yori Dango:
"Our New Relationship"

00:24:05.210 --> 00:24:08.190
I can believe his words now.
